  </details>

  <!-- Press section -->
  <section class="press-section reveal">
    <h2>Press &amp; Media</h2>
    <div class="press-list">

      <article class="press-item">
        <p class="meta">Azusa Pacific University &middot; June 2026 &middot; by Bella Youssefian</p>
        <h3>Faith, Code, and Community in APU's Computer Science Degree</h3>
        <blockquote>
          "We're creating software where students in rural Uganda can build resumes without power or internet access."
        </blockquote>
        <p class="press-body">
          Published while I was actively building the Uganda project. The most current and most technical coverage: quoted directly on the engineering work itself, not just my advocacy history.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="press-item">
        <p class="meta">Diamond Bar-Walnut Patch &middot; April 2024 &middot; by Kelli Gile</p>
        <h3>Getting to Know District of Choice</h3>
        <blockquote>
          "The District of Choice program has opened countless doors for me. I push myself every day to be a better student and person because I know that I have been given an incredible opportunity."
        </blockquote>
        <p class="press-body">
          Featured as the student voice for California's District of Choice program, the same program SB 897 later made permanent.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="press-item">
        <p class="meta">the hoofprint &middot; October 2024 &middot; by Antra Shah</p>
        <h3>California approves new District of Choice bill</h3>
        <p class="press-body">
          Coverage of SB 897 being signed into law, confirming Walnut Valley had more District of Choice students than any district in California.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="press-item">
        <p class="meta">the hoofprint &middot; October 2024 &middot; by Trae Contryman</p>
        <h3>WHS Holds First Student Think Tank of the Year</h3>
        <blockquote>
          "I think a lot of other people were excited as well because there's so many people at Think Tank this year, way bigger than last year."
        </blockquote>
        <p class="press-body">
          Quoted as ASB president and Think Tank member.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="press-item">
        <p class="meta">the hoofprint &middot; November 2024 &middot; by Lydia Chen</p>
        <h3>Students make a difference at the school</h3>
        <p class="press-body">
          Coverage of student organizations' role in school decision-making. Pictured and named as the ASB representative alongside leaders from Student Think Tank, Peer Counseling, and Publications.
        </p>
      </article>

    </div>
  </section>

</div>
